From 3cb36441e50c205b4e9c27ab7fb24565ddc39faf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:21:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/23] ggml, vulkan, glm5-next: fused mHC pre op
 (DSV4_HC_PRE_MIX)

One op per mHC block replaces the flat RMS_NORM, the pre/post affine+sigmoid
chains, HC_COMB, HC_PRE and the following attn/ffn RMS_NORM_MUL. The flat norm
has no weight, so hc_fn*rms_norm(x) = r*(hc_fn*x) and the op applies r itself
(LLAMA_HC_PRE_MIX=nofold keeps the norm before hc_fn, =0 disables the op).
Output: y [n_embd, n_tokens] then a 32-float tail per token with post|comb|r;
DSV4_HC_POST reads post/comb as views. CPU reference, Vulkan shader (one
workgroup per token, subgroup-shuffle sinkhorn as dsv4_hc_comb), probe in
resolve_fused_ops, test-backend-ops cases with GLM shapes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
